    "pathway_role_summary": "WNT3A is a canonical Wnt ligand that initiates beta-catenin-dependent signaling by binding to Frizzled receptors and LRP5/6 co-receptors. This triggers disassembly of the destruction complex, beta-catenin stabilization and nuclear translocation, and activation of TCF/LEF target genes. WNT3A plays essential roles in embryonic development (mesoderm formation, neural tube patterning, somitogenesis), stem cell self-renewal (intestinal crypts), and tissue homeostasis."
