    "data_quality_notes": "High quality data with extensive experimental validation. Multiple cryo-EM structures available showing WNT3A in complex with WLS, PORCN, and trafficking machinery. Comprehensive PTM characterization including critical palmitoleoylation at S209 and glycosylation sites. Extensive disulfide bond network with some bonds predicted by homology to mouse Wnt3a. Binding affinities for Frizzled receptors available (3.6-48.6 nM range), but specific Kd values for LRP5/6 interactions not found. AFM complex has EC50 of 1.67-5 nM. Limited kinetic rate constants (kon/koff) available for most interactions. AlphaFold structure available but detailed confidence metrics could not be accessed.",
    "modeling_relevance_summary": "WNT3A is critical ligand for canonical Wnt pathway modeling. Essential features for modeling: (1) Palmitoleoylation-dependent binding to WLS for secretion, (2) AFM-mediated solubilization and transport in extracellular space, (3) Ternary complex formation with FZD and LRP5/6 receptors (quantitative Kd ~3.6 nM for FZD binding), (4) Regulation by PORCN (palmitoleoylation) and NOTUM (depalmitoleoylation), (5) Inhibition by DKK1, APCDD1, and sFRP proteins, (6) Extensive disulfide bond network that can lead to inactive oligomers if disrupted. The S209 palmitoleoylation site is critical control point for WNT3A activity and trafficking."
